---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { sponsorshipOpen } from '../lib/env';
import { OPERATOR } from '../lib/site';

const open = sponsorshipOpen();
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" crumbLabel="Privacy">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">What we collect, why, and how long we keep it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
    <p>
      {OPERATOR.name}, trading as <a href={OPERATOR.url}>{OPERATOR.tradingAs}</a>, decides how your data is used. Email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>If you just look at events</h2>
    <p>
      We don't use analytics, tracking or adverts. We set one cookie only if you change your
      <a href="/settings">display settings</a>, so the site remembers them.
    </p>
    <h2>If you add an event</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your email address so we can tell you when your event is checked. We never show it on the site. We delete
      it 90 days after the event ends.
    </p>
    <h2>If you subscribe to emails</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your email address and your choices until you unsubscribe. Every email has a link to unsubscribe in one
      click. If you don't confirm your subscription within 7 days, we delete your email address.
    </p>
    <h2>Copies of the emails we send</h2>
    <p>
      We delete copies of the emails we send 90 days after sending them. When you unsubscribe, we delete the emails
      we've sent about your subscription straight away, and stop any that are on their way.
    </p>
    {open && (
      <>
        <h2>If you sponsor calenda11y</h2>
        <p>
          Stripe handles your payment. We keep your name, email address and the details you choose to show on the
          sponsor page. We never see your card details.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
    <h2>Spam protection</h2>
    <p>
      Forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to check you're a person. It doesn't ask you to solve puzzles. Cloudflare may
      process your IP address to do this. We store a scrambled version of IP addresses for up to a day to limit spam.
    </p>
    <h2>If you search near a place</h2>
    <p>
      To find a place you type in "Near", we send just those words to OpenStreetMap's place search (Nominatim, run by
      the OpenStreetMap Foundation). We don't send anything about you. We keep the answer for 30 days so the same search
      isn't sent again, but not who searched. Event addresses are looked up the same way.
    </p>
    <h2>Services we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Vercel hosts the website.</li>
      <li>Supabase stores the data.</li>
      <li>Resend sends emails.</li>
      {open && <li>Stripe takes sponsorship payments.</li>}
      <li>Cloudflare Turnstile protects forms from spam.</li>
      <li>OpenStreetMap's Nominatim finds places for "near me" searches.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a> to ask about your data or to delete it. If you're
      not happy with our answer, you can complain to the
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
